  "solution": {
    "text": "Path of light ray for minimum deviation will be<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0086_c30dcd0db6c8.jpg\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 323px;\" /><br /><math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>°</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>°</mo></math><br />Deviation<math><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>°</mo></math><br />There are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> such deviations therefore total deviation<math><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><mo>°</mo></math>."
